{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/366101-obvious-questions-regarding-vessels-and-relics","id":366101,"title":"Obvious Questions Regarding Vessels and Relics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-10T23:57:13-08:00","id":366101,"title":"Obvious Questions Regarding Vessels and Relics","content":"I feel like these are really stupid questions, but I've been scouring the corebook with no luck and it makes me feel like an idiot.<ul><li>Mechanically, what do Vessels <i>do</i>?</li> <li>Are there mechanics for returning Relics to Duat? Are there benefits for doing so?</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T01:37:26-08:00","id":366159,"title":"","content":"1. Vessel is the catch-all term for a magical item, namely Relics and Vestiges. Do you mean Vestiges?<br /> <br /> 2. I don't believe so. It's basically, &quot;Descent ends, all vessels in tomb that aren't linked to Lifeweb vanish/are drained of all power.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T18:17:16-08:00","id":366786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/366101-obvious-questions-regarding-vessels-and-relics#post366101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there benefits for doing so?</div> </div> </div> </div>There certainly would be at least narrative penalties for a mummy to deny returning the Judges' due to Duat. That is the whole purpose of the Arisen, after all. I could see a Judge accelerating the Descent clock for an Arisen who consistently seeks out relics but secrets them away so the Sekhem is not returned with him when he returns to henet. Or the Judge sending other servants (or other Judges sending their servants) to collect those relics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T02:43:27-08:00","id":367173,"title":"","content":"I'm struggling with these questions a lot myself, as a potential storyteller. I feel like their is something cosmically or narratively unsatisfying in <i>just</i> having the Arisn collect artifacts to return to Duat: it begs the question of &quot;why?&quot; and the answer &quot;because we said so; you will never see any benefit or proof it worked&quot; seems flat to me, and perhaps designed to make the characters want Ascent. It leaves a host of questions unanswered what do Judges do with the Sekhem? What is supposed to happen with Sekhem in Duat? Is the draining of life from the living world leading to anything? What do Vessels mean / how are they made? ... and all of these questions lead to the central one what underpins them: What consequences does this have on the characters and story? &quot;Do it or get smacked&quot; feels very unsatisfying to me, especially as a potential ST, doesn't fit in with the idea of Arisen and Vessels being chess pieces, and while it reinforces the 'Arisen are slaves' theme, gives a somewhat pointless feel to the Arisen existing. I suppose there's a thematic something to be said for &quot;do this task, which means nothing to you, so that I may live&quot;, but I think it undermines the purpose of Judges, Irem, and Arisen existing at all, and makes the concept of rebellion more flat. YMMV though, of course.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm working on a personal setting hack to resolve these issues that I have. My assumptions are that the Judges have the goal of creating a particular kind of civilization (Irem) and that Vessels are their long-term ways to enact that (via Lifeweb). Mind you, this is particular to a chronicle where tradition and adaptability are central themes, and this assumption is very much tailored to that, but I think it provides a more meaningful purpose and conflict (though I admit to understanding the game's assumptions poorly, in terms of Vessels). The hack I'm working on combines Vessels' lifeweb, passive area effects, and sacred geometry in order to bring a more agenda-based purpose to the story. I think I may also include a way to convert Vestiges into Relics (with massive effort), as I likewise don't understand their mechanical benefit.<br /> <br /> Mummy has aspects which really lend itself to answering The Big Questions in the nWoD: How are souls made; Why are there seemingly increasing numbers? What is the purpose of humanity / civilization; How do various Powers manipulate it; Is it worth helping arrange? But it seems to me to back away from these, along with too many other aspects; asking &quot;why&quot; but leaving important gaps. They probably do this for a reason: nWoD is notorious for not answering cosmological questions. and any published answer is likely to not be as satisfying to a chronicle as one created by a storyteller to tailor-fit it (and perhaps detrimental to it). But elements in Mummy create the question, &quot;why&quot;, insinuates that the answer exists <i>and is important</i> to the narrative, and then leaves a noticeable void where any suggestion would be - or, if &quot;it sustains the Judges&quot; is in fact the answer, gives an unsatisfying one (with the possible exception of in a Deceived chronicle).<br /> <br /> This could just be me, and is probably off topic from the OP. but I hope they fill several of these gaps (especially the point and use of Vessels [Vestiges especially]) in an up-coming supplement designed for endgame. There is a certain value to making players answer these things themselves, but I'm struggling with the sense that the book eludes to something <i>important</i> and then delivers a barely consequential cop-out.<br /> I'd really appreciate if someone could help me understand differently. (Especially in a way that helps the OP; sorry for the rant.)<br /> Can someone elaborate these answers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 01-12-2015, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T10:16:04-08:00","id":367489,"title":"","content":"Book Of The Deceived kinda clarifies a lot of things as far as the cosmology of Mummy The Curse is concerned, even if it also brings many more questions. I recommend reading that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:55:19-08:00","id":367619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/366101-obvious-questions-regarding-vessels-and-relics?p=367489#post367489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book Of The Deceived kinda clarifies a lot of things as far as the cosmology of Mummy The Curse is concerned, even if it also brings many more questions. I recommend reading that.</div> </div> </div> </div>*<br /> <br /> *Unless you have no intention of running it, in which case, it's chock-full of Storyteller-only spoilers.<br /> <br /> Not that I think you don't already know this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}